blic","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-01T18:32:17Z","updated_at":"2018-12-01T18:32:17Z","body":"**Jakub Synowiec** has proposed a fix for this issue:\n\n**Fix PostgreSQL reflection of domains expressed as arrays** https://gerrit.sqlalchemy.org/993","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/443447592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/443447900","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4377#issuecomment-443447900","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4377","id":443447900,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MzQ0NzkwMA==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-01T18:36:11Z","updated_at":"2018-12-01T18:36:11Z","body":"\r\n> Managing domains is another topic. One have to write the SQL manually and execute it against the database. I've started experimenting with `_CreateDropBase`, `compiles` decorator and visitors but I'm just exploring some ideas. @zzzeek can you give me some pointers where to look? I would eventually like to have Alembic generating migrations for PSQL domains.\r\n\r\nso if you really want to get into it, it would be nice if Alembic had first class support for PG domains.   as Im sure you know, just to get through the day you can emit `op.execute(\"ALTER ...\")` in any way you'd like to create and alter domains, however to get real operations for them as well as autogenerate support, for starters you can go through the series of steps at first at https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/api/operations.html#operation-plugins and then for autogenerate at https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/api/autogenerate.html#autogen-custom-ops .   If you can get all those things working, that paves the way for them to be included in Alembic fully.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.gith